{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides' arithmetic is right, and it produces no money. On the rider's claim: a deviation IS established. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measurement; EV-GPS-02845 records 4.05 km between the recorded pickup event (2026-09-18T08:43:59) and the recorded dropoff event (08:49:59) against the booked optimal of 3.2 km on EV-TRIP-02845 — an excess of 0.85 km, or 26.56% of optimal. Both establishment limbs pass (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%). The trip_record's actual_distance_km of 4.00 km would give exactly 0.80 km and fail the absolute limb, so the trace figure is the one used, exactly as POL-RD-01 requires. The trace is NOT impaired for policy purposes — 37 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s — so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) and POL-RD-10(3) do not engage, and no independent corroboration is required. On the excusals: EV-CHAT-02845 carries 0 messages, so no POL-RD-04 rider-requested detour can be made out and no distance is excludable. Both amended-endpoint fields on the trip record are null (pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at, amended_optimal_distance_km, amended_optimal_duration_min), so POL-RD-05 relocation does not apply and 3.2 km remains the baseline. vehicle_type is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-12's pooled baseline is not in play. No traffic_advisory covers this window (EV-ADVIS-02845-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and the driver's statement 'Followed the app' asserts no external traffic cause at all, so nothing reduces the measured excess; the absent advisory is not an escalation trigger because no party invoked an exculpatory clause against it (POL-RD-13(1)). On the remedy: the fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs on the booked optimal. Reading the surge multiplier from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (1.0): recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 3.2 + 0.28 × 7.0) × 1.0 + 0.80 = 8.96. charged_total = 9.28. Refund = 9.28 − 8.96 = 0.32, with no ERP, toll, airport surcharge, waiting-time fee or promo discount to add or subtract. 0.32 is below the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor POL-RD-02 sets, so the outcome is NO_ACTION and the 9.28 charge stands as the present state under POL-GEN-03. On the driver's points: the deviation is not MATERIAL (not above 50% and not above 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not triggered and no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) is available; and even if consulted, no pattern is established — deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1/316 completed_trips_90d is about 0.3% (below 5%), so no conduct referral follows. No clause produces a referral here, and no escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fires. Every artifact that carries the deciding fact (EV-GPS-02845, EV-TRIP-02845, EV-FARE-02845) is at weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped below 1.0 and sits well above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect is nil and therefore below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold."
