g.\n\nRemedy (POL-RD-02). The fare is METERED, and the surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 1.0. Recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 3.2 km + 0.28 x 7.0 min) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 8.96. charged_total is 9.28. Refund = 9.28 - 8.96 = 0.32, which is below the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so the outcome is NO_ACTION and the present state stands (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 left as they are). POL-RD-09 adds nothing: there are no ERP gantry lines (optimal_route_erp 0.00) and no airport surcharge, and the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport, so there is no pass-through or billing-integrity correction.\n\nEscalation. The gps_trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c): 100% coverage, 37 fixes at a 10-second interval, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. Trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and no timestamps conflict. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires, so the case is decided rather than escalated, and the confidence cap from POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0 because every artifact carrying the deciding facts is at weight 1.0.",
